findings.suggestion:
Add `method: WorkflowMethods.SMS` to the second OR branch so the retryCount-based cleanup is scoped to SMS rows only:

```typescript
await prisma.workflowReminder.deleteMany({
  where: {
    OR: [
      { method: WorkflowMethods.SMS, scheduledDate: { lte: dayjs().toISOString() } },
      { method: WorkflowMethods.SMS, retryCount: { gt: 1 } },
    ],
  },
});
```

Or equivalently hoist `method` to the top level since both branches now require it:

```typescript
await prisma.workflowReminder.deleteMany({
  where: {
    method: WorkflowMethods.SMS,
    OR: [
      { scheduledDate: { lte: dayjs().toISOString() } },
      { retryCount: { gt: 1 } },
    ],
  },
});
```

This preserves the intended SMS-only cleanup and is robust against future use of `retryCount` on EMAIL/WHATSAPP reminders.

findings.evidence:
END A — apps/web/vercel.json (the ONLY cron config in the repo for the web app that hosts this route):
"crons": [
  { "path": "/api/cron/calendar-cache-cleanup", "schedule": "0 5 * * *" },
  { "path": "/api/tasks/cron", "schedule": "* * * * *" },
  { "path": "/api/tasks/cleanup", "schedule": "0 0 * * *" }
]
— No entry for /api/cron/workflows/scheduleSMSReminders. apps/api/v1/vercel.json has no crons block. grep for scheduleSMS|reminder across all vercel.json files returned no matches. The route exists (apps/web/pages/api/cron/workflows/scheduleSMSReminders.ts: `export { default } from "@calcom/features/ee/workflows/api/scheduleSMSReminders";`) but is scheduled outside the repo, with no overlap guarantee.

END B — packages/features/ee/workflows/api/scheduleSMSReminders.ts:
  line 48-60 (READ, once, into memory):
    const unscheduledReminders = (await prisma.workflowReminder.findMany({
      where: { method: WorkflowMethods.SMS, scheduled: false, scheduledDate: { lte: dayjs().add(7, "day").toISOString() } },
      select: { ...select, retryCount: true },
    })) as (PartialWorkflowReminder & { retryCount: number })[];
  line 159 (external side effect BEFORE any state change):
    const scheduledSMS = await twilio.scheduleSMS(sendTo, message, reminder.scheduledDate, senderID, userId, teamId);
  line 169-177 (non-conditional write of scheduled=true — no WHERE scheduled:false):
    await prisma.workflowReminder.update({
      where: { id: reminder.id },
      data: { scheduled: true, referenceId: scheduledSMS.sid },
    });
  line 179-186 and 190-197 (stale read-modify-write of retryCount — NOT Prisma atomic increment):
    await prisma.workflowReminder.update({
      where: { id: reminder.id },
      data: { retryCount: reminder.retryCount + 1 },
    });
  line 29-45 (top-of-handler deleteMany with no per-row lock):
    await prisma.workflowReminder.deleteMany({
      where: { OR: [ { method: WorkflowMethods.SMS, scheduledDate: { lte: dayjs().toISOString() } }, { retryCount: { gt: 1 } } ] },
    });

No lock, no transaction wrapping read+write, no atomic increment, no compare-and-swap on `scheduled`. grep confirms retryCount is written on WorkflowReminder only in this single file.
